    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Bildad Speaks: God Punishes the Wicked"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Bildad the Shuhite answered and said:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“How long will you hunt for words?",
          "Consider, and then we will speak."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why are we counted as cattle?",
          "Why are we stupid in your sight?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You who tear yourself in your anger,",
          "shall the earth be forsaken for you,",
          "or the rock be removed out of its place?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Indeed, the light of the wicked is put out,",
          "and the flame of his fire does not shine."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The light is dark in his tent,",
          "and his lamp above him is put out."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His strong steps are shortened,",
          "and his own schemes throw him down."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For he is cast into a net by his own feet,",
          "and he walks on its mesh."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A trap seizes him by the heel;",
          "a snare lays hold of him."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A rope is hidden for him in the ground,",
          "a trap for him in the path."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Terrors frighten him on every side,",
          "and chase him at his heels."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His strength is famished,",
          "and calamity is ready for his stumbling."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It consumes the parts of his skin;",
          "the firstborn of death consumes his limbs."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He is torn from the tent in which he trusted",
          "and is brought to the king of terrors."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In his tent dwells that which is none of his;",
          "sulfur is scattered over his habitation."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His roots dry up beneath,",
          "and his branches wither above."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His memory perishes from the earth,",
          "and he has no name in the street."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He is thrust from light into darkness,",
          "and driven out of the world."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He has no posterity or progeny among his people,",
          "and no survivor where he used to live."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They of the west are appalled at his day,",
          "and horror seizes them of the east."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Surely such are the dwellings of the unrighteous,",
          "such is the place of him who knows not God.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
